Day 9 — AWS Monitoring + Observability (CloudWatch, X-Ray, Alarms)

STAR-based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ A production application faces intermittent latency spikes. How will you design monitoring to detect, analyze, and alert on this proactively?

2️⃣ You need centralized monitoring for EC2, Lambda, RDS, and EKS across multiple accounts. How will you architect this using AWS-native tools?

3️⃣ CloudWatch alarms are triggering too frequently, causing alert fatigue. How will you tune thresholds and alarm strategies?

4️⃣ You must monitor custom application metrics not available by default. How will you publish and visualize custom metrics?

5️⃣ Logs from multiple services need to be searched quickly during incidents. How will you structure log groups, retention, and queries?

6️⃣ A Lambda-based application needs end-to-end request tracing across services. How will you implement distributed tracing?

7️⃣ You want alerts only when an error persists for 5 minutes, not on short spikes. How will you configure this in CloudWatch?

8️⃣ A security team needs to track API calls and configuration changes. Which logs will you enable and how will you analyze them?

9️⃣ Application logs are increasing costs rapidly. How will you optimize log ingestion, retention, and filtering?

🔟 You need dashboards showing latency, error rate, throughput, and availability for leadership reviews. How will you design these dashboards?

1️⃣1️⃣ An EC2 instance is running but the application is down. How will you design health checks beyond CPU and memory?

1️⃣2️⃣ You need to detect anomalies automatically without defining static thresholds. Which AWS features will you use?

1️⃣3️⃣ A microservices architecture needs correlation between logs and traces. How will you implement this effectively?

1️⃣4️⃣ Monitoring data must be retained for compliance for more than one year. How will you manage retention and archival?

1️⃣5️⃣ During a major outage, you need a clear incident timeline. How will monitoring and logging help in post-incident analysis?
